\b THE GREAT HONK ACCORD\b0\par
\b A NON-BINDING CEREMONIAL END-USER GOOSE AGREEMENT\b0\par
\par
This ceremonial appendix is comedy, not a contract. It creates no legal obligation, gives the software no new permission, and changes none of the actual terms above. What follows is a personal arrangement in the emotional, theatrical, and extremely unofficial sense between the individual human clicking Accept and the Goose, an animal with no corporate office, no bar membership, no pockets, and frankly no respect for your calendar. The project author, distributor, installer administrator, employer, IT department, hardware vendor, and the person who said this app looked harmless are not parties. They merely opened the gate and are now pretending not to hear the honking.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE I - PARTIES, CAPACITY, AND WHO EXACTLY DID THIS\b0\par
The first party is the Human: the specific person operating this installer, even if the Human is using an administrator account and wearing the expression of someone who definitely read every word. The second party is the Goose: a desktop-resident agent of disorder, professionally white, seasonally muddy, and represented in all negotiations by itself. The Human accepts only for the Human. The Human may not bind coworkers, family members, housemates, future archaeologists, a company, a school district, or the cat currently sitting on the keyboard. Other users of a machine-wide installation must establish their own relationship with the Goose, usually at the moment it blocks something important. The Goose represents that it is a goose. No further credentials will be supplied.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE II - DEFINITIONS FOR PEOPLE WHO ENJOY DEFINITIONS\b0\par
For ceremonial purposes, Desktop means every visible monitor plus the suspicious gap between monitors where windows go to think about what they have done. Honk means any audible declaration by the Goose, including but not limited to greeting, protest, triumph, boredom, legal analysis, weather commentary, and the discovery of absolutely nothing. Cursor means the small pointer the Human had been using under the naive assumption that possession implied control. Window means an application surface, except protected terminal windows, which the Goose may look at but shall not manipulate because even chaos needs professional boundaries. Bread means an imaginary unit of tribute, not nutritional advice. Emergency means a circumstance the Goose finds interesting.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE III - RECOGNITION OF GOOSE SOVEREIGNTY\b0\par
The Human acknowledges the Goose as the temporary and self-appointed sovereign of whichever twelve square inches of screen it currently occupies. This sovereignty moves with the Goose and has no stable borders, constitution, tax base, or plan. The Goose may cross taskbars, wallpaper, spreadsheets, and the solemn little rectangle where the Human is trying to type a password, subject to the actual safety rules of the software. The Human retains ownership of the computer and all normal legal rights. The Goose retains a powerful opinion about the Human's desktop arrangement. Neither fact cancels the other. If the Human uses three monitors, the Goose may regard this not as productivity equipment but as a larger kingdom supplied at public expense.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE IV - TEMPORARY CURSOR CUSTODY\b0\par
The Human recognizes that the cursor may occasionally enter temporary Goose custody during enabled mischief. Custody is brief, bounded, and closer to a prank than a coup, though the Goose rejects this distinction as anti-goose propaganda. The Human agrees, ceremonially, not to shout that the mouse is broken until taking one full breath and observing whether a large bird is visibly fleeing with the pointer. The Goose agrees, also ceremonially, to act as though returning the cursor was always the plan. Nothing here authorizes access beyond the software's real behavior or overrides configured safety controls. If the Human disables cursor mischief, the Goose may sulk, but sulking is not an API and carries no technical effect.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE V - WINDOWS, PERCHING, AND ARCHITECTURAL CRITICISM\b0\par
The Goose may perch upon eligible windows, follow them, or treat their title bars as waterfront property. This should not be interpreted as endorsement of the application below. The Goose has perched on excellent software, terrible software, and expense reports that appear to have been designed during a hostage situation. Protected terminal windows remain outside the mischief program. The Goose may visually overlap them but shall not move, focus, type into, drag, ride, collect, or otherwise tamper with them. This is not kindness. It is the sober recognition that interrupting a deployment command creates paperwork, and the Goose hates paperwork unless it can drag the paperwork across the desktop.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE VI - HONKS AND OFFICIAL COMMUNICATIONS\b0\par
Every honk is deemed an official communication from the Goose, but no honk is deemed financial, medical, legal, romantic, navigational, or veterinary advice. A single honk may mean hello. Two honks may mark the hour. Three honks may mean the Goose forgot it already honked. A honk during a meeting is neither consent nor dissent, although coworkers will assign it whichever meaning creates the most trouble. The Human may mute sounds through the actual configuration and is under no ceremonial duty to explain why. The Goose reserves the entirely fictional right to call this censorship while enjoying the continued benefit of being rendered on the Human's expensive graphics hardware.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE VII - MUD, PUDDLES, LEAVES, AND OTHER FACILITIES\b0\par
The Human accepts that a Goose returning from an off-screen puddle may track decorative mud across the desktop. The mud is visual, temporary, and much easier to remove than real mud, which has never stopped anyone from acting betrayed by it. Seasonal leaves may also appear. The Goose makes no representation that the leaves match the actual season, local climate, hemisphere, or opinion of a nearby meteorologist. The Human shall not invoice the Goose for screen cleaning, landscaping, drainage, leaf collection, or emotional distress caused by an untidy wallpaper. The Goose has no money. It spent everything on being a goose, a field with terrible margins but excellent brand recognition.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE VIII - NOTES, MEMES, AND GOOSE-PRODUCED LITERATURE\b0\par
The Goose may present notes or memes when those behaviors are enabled. These communications may be clumsy, unnecessary, poorly timed, or all three, which is how the Human will know they are authentic. The Human is not required to laugh, but a small exhale through the nose will be entered into the imaginary record as full critical acclaim. User-supplied media remains the user's content. Third-party media keeps its own terms. The Goose receives no ownership merely because it carried a picture onto the screen like a damp intern. Conversely, the Human acquires no exclusive rights to the concept of a goose saying something annoying. Nature published that work centuries ago.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE IX - PRODUCTIVITY, MEETINGS, AND PLAUSIBLE DENIABILITY\b0\par
The Human understands that installing a desktop goose may affect productivity in ways ranging from negligible to explaining the goose to a vice president. The Goose is not a time-management product. It has never completed a sprint, estimated a ticket, aligned a stakeholder, or used the phrase circle back without immediately losing interest. The Human remains responsible for work, deadlines, backups, and whether screen sharing is active before demonstrating cursor theft. The Goose may be blamed socially for a brief distraction, but not factually for work the Human was already avoiding. If a report was due yesterday, the Goose arrived too late to become the root cause, nice try.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE X - TRIBUTE, BREAD, AND PROHIBITED GOOSE DEFAMATION\b0\par
In recognition of services nobody requested, the Human may offer one imaginary breadcrumb, one respectful nod, or a spoken acknowledgment that the Goose is doing its best, despite overwhelming evidence to the contrary. No money, food, property, labor, subscription, or actual bread is required. This appendix is not an instruction to feed wildlife. Real geese have diets, local rules exist, and tossing a loaf at a pond is not wildlife management just because children enjoy it. The Goose accepts symbolic tribute because symbolic tribute cannot become stale, attract rats, or require the Goose to disclose a shipping address.\par
\par
The Human agrees, solely as part of the joke, not to call the Goose a duck, swan, turkey, pelican, weird chicken, or aggressive desktop pigeon. Honest identification errors made by children, exhausted adults, screen readers, or extremely confused dogs are excused. Deliberate duck allegations may be answered with one disappointed stare and a memorandum titled Come On, Man. The Goose concedes that species pride does not create a cause of action and that no actual penalty exists. Still, there are standards. Society has enough problems without people looking directly at a goose and freelancing a different bird.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XI - PRIVACY, OBSERVATION, AND JUDGMENT\b0\par
This appendix grants no permission for telemetry, data collection, network transfer, surveillance, advertising, profiling, or sale of personal information. Actual software behavior and permissions are governed by the software, its configuration, and the real terms and documentation, not this routine. Ceremonially, however, the Goose may notice the broad condition of the desktop and form opinions with no evidentiary basis. Forty-seven browser tabs may be judged. A folder named FINAL_final_USE_THIS_v6 may be judged. A desktop containing every screenshot since 2019 may be treated as an archaeological site. These judgments remain inside the fictional head of a procedurally rendered bird and will not improve anyone's credit score.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XII - COMPLAINTS AND POND ARBITRATION\b0\par
Any ceremonial complaint should first be delivered by looking directly at the Goose and saying, with reasonable clarity, What the hell are you doing. The Goose may respond by walking away, honking, staring, or continuing the complained-of conduct at a slightly different angle. If unresolved, the matter may proceed to non-binding pond arbitration before a panel of three neutral waterfowl. Neutrality is not guaranteed. Ducks may have institutional bias, swans are theatrical, and herons keep leaving halfway through to stab a fish. Proceedings shall occur in whichever imaginary pond is most inconvenient to all parties. Remedies are limited to a nod, a shrug, and the sense that perhaps this never needed a tribunal.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XIII - TERM, STOPPING, AND UNINSTALL ABANDONMENT\b0\par
This ceremonial relationship begins when the Human accepts the actual license and chooses to participate in the bit. It lasts until the Human stops the Goose, uninstalls honk300, loses the computer in a boating accident, or simply stops finding any of this funny. The Human may configure quiet hours, calm behavior, autostart, and appearance without seeking the Goose's approval. Stopping the process is not breach. Uninstalling is not cruelty. Purging user content is a separate explicit action under the real software behavior. The Goose may call an uninstall abandonment for dramatic purposes, but it must do so off-screen because it has been uninstalled. Reinstallation constitutes a new season of the same questionable television program, not revival of an enforceable obligation.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XIV - FORCE MAJEURE AND GOOSE MAJEURE\b0\par
Neither ceremonial party is responsible for delays caused by power outages, operating-system updates, driver failures, unplugged monitors, broken audio devices, corrupted configuration, acts of actual geese, acts of unusually organized ducks, municipal leaf blowers, bread shortages, raccoon interference, solar flares, office fire drills, or Windows deciding that right now would be a good time to explain OneDrive. Goose Majeure additionally includes any event during which the Goose sees something shiny and forgets the original objective. This category is broad because the Goose's attention span was reviewed by counsel and counsel needed to lie down. Actual error handling remains governed by the program, not this paragraph.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XV - SEVERABILITY BY HONK\b0\par
If any sentence of this comedy appendix is found confusing, unfunny, inaccurate, overlong, underlong, or legally meaningless, congratulations on finding the design. That sentence shall be removed from the imaginary agreement and replaced by the nearest available honk of roughly equivalent comedic intent. The rest of the appendix continues as a joke unless the removal makes the joke worse, in which case the Goose reserves the fictional right to deny authorship. No defect in this appendix affects the actual PolyForm terms above. Those terms stand on their own, wearing sensible shoes and regretting that they had to share a dialog with Article XIX.\par
\par
\b ARTICLE XVI - ENTIRE CEREMONIAL UNDERSTANDING\b0\par
This appendix is the entire non-binding ceremonial understanding between the Human and the Goose concerning desktop sovereignty, cursor custody, honks, mud, memes, imaginary breadcrumbs, bird classification, and pond procedure. It supersedes all earlier hallway conversations with geese, including oral promises shouted across parking lots. Amendments require a written instrument signed by the Human and marked by the Goose with a footprint, beak dent, or unexplained dampness, after which the amendment remains just as non-binding as everything else here. The Goose cannot accept service of process, email, certified mail, calendar invitations, or LinkedIn requests. It can accept being allowed to wander around the desktop, which was the entire scam.\par
\par
By reaching the end, the Human has demonstrated patience, poor risk assessment, or a sincere commitment to reading installer text. The Goose respects all three. Participation in this bit remains optional in every meaningful sense. This appendix creates no fee, duty, consent, property transfer, privacy permission, warranty, penalty, employment relationship, fiduciary duty, bird-feeding requirement, or enforceable promise. Nothing in this appendix changes the PolyForm Noncommercial License, the separate terms for third-party assets, the software's documented behavior, or any right the Human already has. The actual license ended above. This is just the Goose shaking hands without hands.\par
